ol they're  given an allowance of about 40 pounds a  week but they don't have the right to  work so i i think in terms of the kind  of wide picture  it's been a long year but even those who  have come on those resettlement schemes  some of those are not happy and from the  perspective of the home office it's an  enormous thing to try and and bring  people from afghanistan whereas the  mld's concerned or from the home office  to resettle people  even after this lengthy period of time  it's a very very tricky issue to solve  obviously the speed of the taliban  takeover was remarkable and the need to  get people out of the country in such a  short period of time was unexpected  however it also seems clear that there  was an underestimate on the numbers who  could qualify and of course the whole  process continues  on the next episode of out of  afghanistan we ask about integration for  the resettled refugees how easy is it to  adjust to life in britain and why is it  harder for some than others  how easy is it to make friends in a new  country  out of afghanistan was presented by me  stuart ramsey it was produced by anne  marie bullock sound designed by will  chalk and paul stanworth is the editor  you
 

